stereo-matplotlib (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial package (ORDER 50 step 4): the stereo module of 2026-10-05 (build tree sparky-os/upstream/matplotlib,
    mpl_parallel_stereo.py) made a package of its own, outside Matplotlib. The cameras' offset is fitted to the
    person's depth limits (the largest offset for which every point the figure draws stays inside them) in place
    of the old eye_separation and screen_distance; orthographic plots get the shear about the camera target;
    interactive figures in Tk and Qt (X11) windows show their 3D area as a declared pair with Enable 3D and the
    3D display settings; stills are written as .pns (sTER) and .jps (the stereo layer's JPS block), only to new
    files.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:00:00 -0300
